From: Shivam Mathur <shivam_jpr@hotmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Retain ZEND_RETURN_VALUE for PECL compatibility

PHP master removed this 0-valued arginfo macro in php/php-src#25078.
PECL PSR 1.2.0 still uses it, including when installed directly with pecl.
Keep its original value in the distributed PHP 8.7 headers until the
released extension no longer requires it. ZEND_RETURNS_VALUE is unrelated
and must not be used as a replacement.

--- a/Zend/zend_compile.h
+++ b/Zend/zend_compile.h
@@ -575,6 +575,11 @@ struct _zend_op_array {
 	void *reserved[ZEND_MAX_RESERVED_RESOURCES];
 };
 
+/* Temporary compatibility for PECL PSR 1.2.0 and older releases. */
+#ifndef ZEND_RETURN_VALUE
+# define ZEND_RETURN_VALUE 0
+#endif
+
 #define INTERNAL_FUNCTION_PARAMETERS zend_execute_data *execute_data, zval *return_value
 #define INTERNAL_FUNCTION_PARAM_PASSTHRU execute_data, return_value
 
